==Russian==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*gradъ}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*greh₃d-}}. Cognate with {{cog|li|grúodas}} ({{cog|ine-bsl-pro|*grōda-}}), {{cog|la|grandō}}, {{cog|xcl|կարկուտ}}, Old Indic *hrādúniṣ, and possibly with {{cog|en|grind}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA}}

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+|n=sg}}

# {{lb|ru|meteorology}} [[hail]]
#: {{ru-ux|Град [[идти|идёт]]|It’s hailing.|inline=y}}
# [[volley]], [[shower]]
#: {{ru-ux|град [[пуля|пуль]]|hail of bullets|inline=y}}

=====Declension=====
{{ru-noun-table|n=sg}}

===Etymology 2===
{{bor|ru|cu|градъ|sc=Cyrs|tr=grádŭ}}, which is a reflex of {{der|ru|sla-pro|*gordъ||settlement, enclosed place}}, whence also {{cog|ru|го́род}} was normally inherited by [[w:pleophony|pleophony]]. Old Church Slavonic word shows [[w:liquid metathesis|liquid metathesis]] characteristic of South Slavic area.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA}}

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+}}

# {{lb|ru|pоetic|antiquated}} [[town]], [[city]], used as a common city name suffix ([[Волгоград]], [[Калининград]], [[Ленинград]])
#: {{ru-ux|[[стольный]] град|capital (city) (''modern Russian'': {{m|ru|столица}})|inline=y}}

=====Declension=====
{{ru-noun-table}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ru|го́род}}

===Etymology 3===
{{bor|ru|la|gradus}}.

====Noun====
{{ru-noun|град.|m-in|-}}

# {{ru-abbrev of|гра́дус||[[degree]]}}

[[Category:ru:Weather]]

